      "id": "STU-001",
      "location": "sections/60-history.tex:22, Gospel dossier explanatory row; retained author-proof.pdf p. 17",
      "problem": "The NABRE comparison is paraphrased as dating Matthew after Jerusalem's destruction, \"probably in the following decade.\" The inspected USCCB Matthew introduction instead says \"probably at least a decade later\" than A.D. 70 (https://bible.usccb.org/bible/matthew/0, final authorship/source/date discussion; also the registered matthew-introduction passage and research acquisition matthew-intro.txt:813). The study changes an open minimum interval into a particular following decade, potentially placing composition earlier and adding an unsupported upper bound. The generated comparison correctly retains only the post-A.D. 70 claim, so it does not authorize this narrowing.",
      "repair_target": "study",
      "required_result": "Revise this source-attributed prose to preserve the NABRE introduction's actual qualification: after A.D. 70, probably at least a decade later. Retain the separate critical-profile comparison, Antioch's qualified status, and the distinction from traditional hypotheses; do not invent a replacement year or closed date range.",
      "severity": "blocking"
    }
  ],
